{"type":"standard","title":"Laura Gillen","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laura Gillen</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q131105202","titles":{"canonical":"Laura_Gillen","normalized":"Laura Gillen","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Laura Gillen</span></span>"},"pageid":70218481,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gillen_Laura_119th_Congress_%28cropped2%29.jpg/330px-Gillen_Laura_119th_Congress_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":424},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/Gillen_Laura_119th_Congress_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2240,"height":2877},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374216251","tid":"71d444ea-ad2f-11f1-8b88-16d6e5b85317","timestamp":"2026-09-10T15:51:11Z","description":"American politician and attorney (born 1969)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Gillen","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Gillen?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Gillen?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laura_Gillen"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Gillen","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Laura_Gillen","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Gillen?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Laura_Gillen"}},"extract":"Laura Anne Gillen is an American politician and attorney serving as the U.S. representative for New York's 4th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, she previously served as the town supervisor of Hempstead, New York. Her district includes central and southern Nassau County, a suburban area on Long Island.","extract_html":"<p><b>Laura Anne Gillen</b> is an American politician and attorney serving as the U.S. representative for New York's 4th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, she previously served as the town supervisor of Hempstead, New York. Her district includes central and southern Nassau County, a suburban area on Long Island.</p>"}